  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: infinite loop and deadlock when parsing tar archives\n     with negative member offsets\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-8194.patch: reject negative byte counts in\n       TarInfo._block() with InvalidHeaderError in Lib/tarfile.py, so a\n       crafted negative member size can no longer move the read offset\n       backwards; add regression tests to Lib/test/test_tarfile.py\n     - CVE-2025-8194\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory race condition in ssl.SSLContext\n     cert_store_stats() and get_ca_certs()\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2024-0397.patch: add an X509_STORE_get1_objects()\n       shim that takes a locked deep copy of the certificate store objects\n       and use it in cert_store_stats() and get_ca_certs() in Modules/_ssl.c,\n       so certificates loaded concurrently can no longer free objects that\n       are being iterated\n     - CVE-2024-0397",
